Subject: [PATCH] sycl: opt-in Battlemage kernel choices on Arc A-series (DG2)

Local candidate. GGML_SYCL_DG2_BMG_TUNING is a bit mask (default 0 = upstream behavior):
1 FA quantized-KV decode on TILE, 2 FA VEC 256 threads, 4 q5_K MMVQ reuse,
8 D=256 single-query decode on VEC (PR 30606), 16 q4_K row pairing to 8 columns (needs C30).
Each gate only selects between kernels that are already compiled for every device.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp
index dd599e5a..33b00248 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp
@@ -830,6 +830,23 @@ inline bool ggml_sycl_dnnl_has_optimized_gemm(int device) {
 
 int ggml_sycl_get_env(const char *env_name, int default_val);
 
+// Arc A-series (DG2) opt-in for kernel choices upstream enables on Battlemage only.
+// GGML_SYCL_DG2_BMG_TUNING is a bit mask; 0 (default) keeps upstream behavior.
+enum ggml_sycl_dg2_bmg_tuning_bit {
+    GGML_SYCL_DG2_FA_QKV_TILE   = 1,  // quantized-KV decode (1-2 tokens) on FA TILE instead of VEC
+    GGML_SYCL_DG2_FA_VEC_256    = 2,  // FA VEC with 256-thread work-groups instead of 128
+    GGML_SYCL_DG2_Q5K_REUSE     = 4,  // q5_K multi-column MMVQ weight reuse and fused gate/up
+    GGML_SYCL_DG2_FA_D256_VEC   = 8,  // D=256 single-query decode on FA VEC (PR 30606)
+    GGML_SYCL_DG2_Q4K_WIDE_PAIR = 16, // q4_K MMVQ row pairing up to 8 columns (PR 30226)
+};
+
+static inline bool ggml_sycl_dg2_bmg_tuning(gpu_arch arch, int bit) {
+    static const int mask = ggml_sycl_get_env("GGML_SYCL_DG2_BMG_TUNING", 0);
+    const bool dg2 = arch == gpu_arch::intel_gpu_acm_g10 || arch == gpu_arch::intel_gpu_acm_g11 ||
+                     arch == gpu_arch::intel_gpu_acm_g12;
+    return dg2 && (mask & bit) != 0;
+}
+
